module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_nullary_callable_field_call_is_typed_as_the_callable

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, RungRead, FoundOnRung, AtCeiling }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }

data a_nullary_callable_field_call_is_typed_as_the_callable: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_nullary_callable_field_call_is_typed_as_the_callable" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, standing: AtCeiling { rung: StructurallyGuaranteed, ceiling_reason: "structurally guaranteed (rung 3) on the v1 checker path: the type of a field read as an operation is decided by the field type's callability (v1.compiler.infer_types applied_field_type over type_node_is_callable), so no accepted program contains a nullary field call typed as its callable; it cannot reach 4 while a field-as-operation is a field read whose application is judged afterwards rather than an application node by construction." as NonEmptyStr } },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a record field declared `f: fn() -> T` is called with no arguments, `x.f()`, as a named argument (`consume(a: x.f())`) or bound by a let and then consumed (`let v = x.f()` then `consume(a: v)`), and the checker types the call as the field's own value, `Callable(-> T)`, instead of its application, T. The same call as a match scrutinee is typed T, and a unary field call (`g: fn(A) -> T`, `x.g(a)`) is typed T in every position.",

    "HARM: a correct program is refused. The refusal is `type mismatch: expected 'T', got 'Callable(->T)'`, typed and located, on the ordinary compile (so no witness in the closure runs) and on the seed's [rust] compile before rustc. Every record of operations with a nullary operation (an observe, a keys, a delete over a store's own closed-over state) is therefore unwritable in the natural form, and the shape gets avoided rather than written: the sealed-store lane's own-operations records hit it first (below). Nothing is silently accepted: the measured positions either type the call correctly or refuse.",

    "SCOPE IS THE SHARED CHECKER, NOT ONE TARGET. The first sighting was the [rust] emission of an instrument and read as an emitter defect; the same branch's ordinary compile through claim_batch then refused 32 witnesses of one module at the same shape, so the defect sits before any target realization.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the field's arity and the call's position are the discriminators, not effects, names or records. Renaming the field (remove -> delete_marker) changed nothing; a pure nullary field in the fixture refuses as an effectful one did on the branch; a unary field of the same record types correctly in the same positions; a match over the nullary call refuses an unrelated coproduct's arms exactly as over the unary call, so the scrutinee position is typed as the application.",

    "RECEIPTS, 2026-10-24, proud-boar-59 (the C-deploy sealed-store cohort). (a) BuildBuddy invocation 93a07a90-bec2-495c-b850-afb945cbec28, `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:native-emission-controls` with an uncommitted case: `V2-NATIVE REFUSAL cause=EmissionRefused stage=emit -- ... [rust] produced 1 hard diagnostic(s): type mismatch: expected 'Coproduct(ProbeWrite)', got 'Callable(->Coproduct(ProbeWrite))'` at `probe_written(w: store.remove())`. A rerun with the field renamed refused identically, and a third with the call let-bound refused at the let. (b) The same branch's ordinary compile through claim_batch refused 32 witnesses of test.claim.deploy_transition_witness with `type mismatch: expected 'Coproduct(FilesystemFileObservation)', got 'Callable(->Coproduct(FilesystemFileObservation))'` at `transition_file_observation_of(observed: inhibition.observe())`. (c) test.claim.nullary_field_call_typing_witness over self-contained fixture modules on main cce148f52a9: a first cut (BuildBuddy invocation 196a160d-9457-4420-8707-f7827dec4ded) expected a match over the nullary call to ADMIT foreign arms and that probe FAILED with a blocking delta of 2, so it became the control that the scrutinee is typed correctly; the filed witness then ran 6 PASS / 0 FAIL (claim_batch exit 0, BuildBuddy invocation 623d0368-12a8-40ae-a954-7c1b7dc9e917).",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- the wrong type is never acted on; it surfaces only as a typed, located refusal (of a correct program). It is still a floor failure (DESIGN section 4b: values inhabit declared types, and the checker's own reading of a call is wrong). CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- the call's type is decidable from the field's declared type. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the capability named in the rung field. Executing evidence: test.claim.nullary_field_call_typing_witness, whose two expecting-red probes are inverted, not deleted, when it lands.",

    "POPULATION, FOUND BY GREP AND THEREFORE A LOWER BOUND: at main cce148f52a9 one nullary callable field is called, `extdeps.mercurial` `mercurial_repository_completeness_fold`, `MercurialContentsComplete => fold.complete()` over `complete: fn() -> R`, a match-arm result typed against the function's type parameter R. It is accepted; whether R's binding is what hides the mistype there is NOT measured. The sealed-store lane's own-operations records (gunb-ai/gunbc#14944's SlotStore `keys: fn() -> CasSlotKeys`, matched as a scrutinee in gunbc.compute.attempt_lifecycle) bring the scrutinee form when they land. A nullary field call in a named-argument or let position cannot exist in an accepted module today, which is the refusal half doing its damage: the shape is avoided rather than written.",
    "REPAIRED, 2026-10-24, calm-wren-394 (chain re-derivation, DESIGN section 6b). The earliest unjustified boundary is v1.compiler.infer_lookup product_field_result_type, whose contract is the type an application of the field produces: it decided callability by `params |> count > 0`, so a nullary Arrow answered itself. Parse (make_call_expr keeps the application as an ExprMethodCall) and the ExprMethodCall arm (which takes the lookup's answer) are sound. It is a sibling leaf of gunbc.recurring_failure_mode arity_proxy_for_callability_misroutes_a_found_local: the predicate that row repaired, type_node_is_callable, was never asked here. ROOT GENERALIZATION, the fork census: three leaves read a field as an operation by arity -- product_field_result_type (method calls, and record_field_type_is_unresolved_param through it), the binary-operator algebra-field arm of v1.compiler.infer_types infer_arithmetic_binop_type_node (the same read copied inline), and declared_arg_types_for_method's argument contract (a nullary field had no contract instead of the empty one). All three now route through one rule, v1.compiler.infer_types applied_field_type, and the inline copy is deleted. Not leaves: callable_return_type's nullary arm already reads the codomain, the ExprCall body-local seam is already on type_node_is_callable, and v2.compiler.infer decides a field's operation by the Arrow connective. EXECUTED, test.claim.nullary_field_call_typing_witness widened to 18 cells (claim_batch --hermetic): against the pre-repair seed mirror (BuildBuddy invocation 61fdf304-9c45-4dee-af91-9d49204225ee) five cells refuse with a blocking delta of 1 -- named argument, let binding, positional argument, an alias-typed field and a nested receiver -- and the other 13 hold; against the re-emitted mirror (BuildBuddy invocation d870b211-0bd6-4955-b143-f47fd98b9ce1) all 18 hold, and the stage0 regen reaches first_generation_equal=true in the same run. Five sibling positions were ALREADY admitted before the repair and so do not discriminate it: return, record-literal field, method argument, list element, and a field read off the call's result. They stay enrolled as controls. Those positions admitted a node typed as the callable because they never compare an Arrow with a nominal declared type. That is gunbc.recurring_failure_mode function_typed_argument_mismatch_accepted, still open there (receipt added to that row), and not this row's class.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "extdeps.mercurial", decl_name: "mercurial_repository_completeness_fold", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer_types", decl_name: "applied_field_type", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer_lookup", decl_name: "product_field_result_type", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.nullary_field_call_typing_witness", decl_name: "a_nullary_field_call_as_a_named_argument_is_admitted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.nullary_field_call_typing_witness", decl_name: "a_nullary_field_call_of_a_foreign_codomain_refuses", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
